    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div>p &lt;- ggplot(mtcars, aes(mpg, wt)) + geom_point()</div><div><br></div><div># Calculate correlation for each group</div><div>cors &lt;- ddply(mtcars, c(&quot;vs&quot;, &quot;am&quot;), summarise, cor = round(cor(mpg, wt), 2))</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>p + facet_grid(vs ~ am) +</div><div>  geom_text(data=cors, aes(label=paste(&quot;r=&quot;, cor, sep=&quot;&quot;)), x=30, y=4)</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>I don&#39;t think it&#39;s possible to make this come out correctly with margins=TRUE, though. If you want the margins, you may need to preprocess your data to add an ALL value for each faceting variable.</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>-Winston</div><div><br></div><br></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
